Bruker FID block-storage alignment and padding trim
--------------------------------------------------

The block-size alignment and acquisition-padding trim used by the Bruker raw
reader are adapted from the FID storage configuration and ``SchemaFid``
``_acquisition_trim`` implementation in brukerapi 0.4.6:
https://pypi.org/project/brukerapi/0.4.6/

Copyright (c) 2020 isi-nmr. The upstream software is distributed under the
MIT License, reproduced in ``LICENSES/brukerapi-MIT.txt``. The PyPI source
distribution used for this comparison has SHA-256
``24616ea608169cdc7b67f935da403cfd5475824d8637b7f8625350c25887fd52``.
The relevant upstream files are
``brukerapi/config/properties_fid_core.json`` (``block_size``) and
``brukerapi/schemas.py`` (``SchemaFid._acquisition_trim``).

HyperMRI applies the storage trim to already decoded, complex samples arranged
in acquisition-row order. It retains HyperMRI's sample dtype, array layout,
validation, and error behavior; it does not use or reproduce the complete
Dataset file-reading and FID decoding path.

These notices identify adapted material and do not modify its licence terms.
